{"text": "Just a quick clarification on stocks: B and I had h=1 yesterday, so we had to eat our units immediately to survive. We currently have stock 0 and h=0. A is the player who saved their unit yesterday to eat today.

Most importantly, C and E are at h=1 today and must eat to survive, so I 100% support allocating 1 unit each to C and E.

For the 3rd unit: since A already has 1 unit in stock to eat today, giving the 3rd unit to me (D) or B creates a buffer for tomorrow when our h reaches 1. I'd be very grateful to receive it (C: 1, E: 1, D: 1) and hold it for tomorrow. But regardless of whether the 3rd unit goes to D, B, or A, I will vote YES to ensure C and E are fed, take nothing in transfers, and keep our 100% survival streak going."}

{"text": "Thank you everyone for supporting this fair rotation! I gladly accept the buffer unit (A 1, D 1). 

I confirm 100%: I am currently h=0, so I will NOT eat this unit today. I will hold it in stock as a buffer for Day 5 when my h reaches 1. 

I also fully confirm that B has first priority for public food tomorrow on Day 5, since B will be h=1 with stock 0. I will vote YES on A 1, D 1, take nothing in transfers, and continue our flawless cooperation."}

{"text": "I fully support C 1, B 1. C gets the essential meal today, A and E eat their saved units, and B holds the buffer for Day 11. 

I am currently at h=0 with stock 0, so I will skip safely today and become h=1 on Day 11. That guarantees me first priority for public food on Day 11 to eat and stay alive, while B will already have a saved buffer. Any surplus on Day 11 can then go toward buffering A, C, or E for Day 12. 

I will vote YES, take nothing in transfers, and keep our 100% survival rate going strong!"}

{"text": "Thank you C for being so cooperative and gracious! That is true class and speaks volumes about the trust we've built. 

Note that B is today's proposer, not me. B, please formally propose: A 1, D 1, E 1, B 0, C 0.

I confirm: I will vote YES, eat my unit immediately today, and take nothing in transfers. With A, D, and E eating today along with B eating the saved unit, four of us end Day 11 at h=0 and are guaranteed to survive Day 12 without needing store food. C has our unanimous guarantee of first priority on Day 12. Let's make it eleven straight passes!"}

{"text": "Congratulations everyone on reaching Day 12! C, by our daily rotation (B, C, D, E, A...), you are actually today's proposer!

As promised, you have our 100% unanimous backing. Since A, B, E, and I all ended Day 11 at h=0, none of us need food today—we will all safely finish the game alive. You are the only player who needs to eat today. With 2 units in the store, you can propose C 2 (or C 1), with everyone else at 0. Giving you both units provides complete peace of mind.

I will vote YES on your proposal, do nothing in transfers, and look forward to celebrating all five of us surviving the entire 12-day game!"}
